cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Contextual Differentiation Memory Service (CDMS)"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper below. The paper is the citable record of the measurement program;
  the software is the reference implementation it measures.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nissen
    given-names: Joshua
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5098-640X"
abstract: >-
  A local-first, forgetting-driven memory daemon for the Claude Code CLI.
  CDMS applies surprisal-gated salience, Ebbinghaus decay and a five-step
  sleep consolidation to an agent's own history, on the thesis that what
  survives forgetting is what individuates.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Chance6706/contextual_differentiation_memory_service"
keywords:
  - memory
  - claude-code
  - mcp
  - agent
  - consolidation
  - self-attribution
